WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.520
Strawberries, mushrooms, bacteria and people all have DNA.

2
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:15.400
How can one kind of molecule help make such different living things?

3
00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:21.220
How can a tiny code inside my cells decide what I look like?

4
00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:24.133
DNA is a molecule.

5
00:00:24.973 --> 00:00:27.533
It carries the instructions for building proteins.

6
00:00:28.633 --> 00:00:30.613
Its shape is a twisted ladder.

7
00:00:31.413 --> 00:00:33.873
This shape is called a double helix.

8
00:00:34.733 --> 00:00:37.693
The two sides of the ladder are sugar and phosphate.

9
00:00:38.633 --> 00:00:41.253
The sides are the same in every living thing.

10
00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:44.967
The code sits in the rungs.

11
00:00:45.607 --> 00:00:49.747
Each rung is a base pair: two bases joined in the middle.

12
00:00:50.707 --> 00:00:59.167
The four bases have letter names: A, T, C and G. A always pairs with T.

13
00:00:59.867 --> 00:01:01.847
C always pairs with G.

14
00:01:02.707 --> 00:01:11.407
So if one side reads A, C, G, T, the other side reads T, G, C, A.

15
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.300
The order of the bases is called the sequence.

16
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.620
The sequence is the code.

17
00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.600
A different order gives different instructions.

18
00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:22.880
Think of letters in a word.

19
00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:26.600
The same letters in a new order spell a new word.

20
00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.580
But a cell does not understand words.

21
00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.160
Its molecules simply follow the bases in order.

22
00:01:33.983 --> 00:01:37.423
DNA is very long and thin.

23
00:01:38.423 --> 00:01:43.083
A chromosome is a strand of DNA wound up tightly with proteins.

24
00:01:44.123 --> 00:01:46.323
A gene is a section of a chromosome.

25
00:01:47.203 --> 00:01:50.263
A gene carries the code for a particular protein.

26
00:01:51.183 --> 00:01:54.823
A protein builds cells and does most of the work in cells.

27
00:01:55.883 --> 00:01:57.243
Proteins affect traits.

28
00:01:57.243 --> 00:02:01.443
A trait is a feature of a living thing, like flower colour.

29
00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:07.807
In pea plants, purple flowers need a working protein from one gene.

30
00:02:08.447 --> 00:02:11.747
A change in that gene can stop the protein from working.

31
00:02:12.267 --> 00:02:14.007
Then the flowers come out white.

32
00:02:15.027 --> 00:02:20.027
So how do strawberries, mushrooms, bacteria and people differ?

33
00:02:20.867 --> 00:02:25.887
They all build DNA from the same sugar, phosphate and four bases.

34
00:02:26.827 --> 00:02:31.087
The order of the bases differs, so their genes code for different proteins.
